{# Repair - Cryosurgical Handpiece (Figma 35098:39248, the client's 1600px frame on the WIP page); the URL is the
   live site's. No redesigned or phone frame exists, so the sections use the redesign's components and type scale, as
   on Micro Instrument Repair:
   - Hero: the shared content hero with the frame's photo and fade, the title, the frame's intro (drawn under the
     hero in Figma) and, as in the frame, the orange "Download Repair Form" button, the page's one download of the
     form (with the download icon rather than Figma's arrow). No Request a Repair strip under the prices.
   - "Typical Repair Charges": the frame's three level cards with the micro price tables' look (navy header, 1px
     #dde7ee border, 4px corners). Under them the warranty line as a notice bar.
   - No Free Lifetime Repair band: cryosurgical handpieces are excluded from the programme.
   - "SEO Text": the PLP features list (bold lead-in, orange dashes).
   - "Disclaimers": a callout where the frame has them, the brands line as its title.
   - FAQ: the shared FAQ section; it loads closed (Figma's orange question is a hover example) and the answers
     are the live page's. #}
{% import "macros/ui.njk" as ui with context %}
{% import "content/macros.njk" as c with context %}
{% import "plp/macros.njk" as plp_ui with context %}
{% set cr = contentPages.cryo %}

{{ ui.breadcrumbs([{ label: "Repair Services", href: "/repair-services/" }, { label: "Cryosurgical Handpiece" }]) }}

{# Hero: the handpieces photo (blue all over) under the frame's fade (cryoFade). From xl the photo is Figma's
   1849x693 (the screen's width from 1849px, so it always reaches the right edge), with the probe tip (43.7% across
   the photo) 60px past the 593px text column: never left of 123px before the screen's edge, which puts the tip at
   685px up to 1600px. From lg to xl it is 1550px wide with the tip at 685px, so more of the handpieces fits beside
   the text and the photo still covers the taller hero. The photo is centred on the hero's height a little high (54%),
   which keeps both handpieces in view on wide screens (Figma's 107px above the hero at 1600). Phones and tablets
   have no room beside the text: the photo covers the hero with the handpieces on the right, under the phone fade
   (also on tablets, where cryoFade would cover all of it) and a 60% navy tint that keeps the white text readable
   over the light blue. The button is full width on phones, like the Home hero's. #}
{% call c.hero({
  title: "Cryosurgical Handpiece Repair", text: cr.intro, figma: "35098:39315", image: "077f3d82",
  fade: contentPages.gradients.cryoFade, fadeAt: "lg",
  photo: "inset-0 h-full w-full object-cover object-[80%_70%] lg:inset-auto lg:left-[8px] lg:top-1/2 lg:h-auto lg:w-[1550px] lg:max-w-none lg:-translate-y-[54%] xl:left-[max(-123px,calc(50%_-_115px_-_max(808px,43.7%)))] xl:w-[max(1849px,100%)]",
  scrim: "bg-primary-500/60 lg:hidden"
}) %}
  <a href="#" data-proto class="btn-accent w-full whitespace-nowrap pr-[30px] md:w-auto" data-figma="35098:39318">Download Repair Form{% icon "download" %}</a>
{% endcall %}

{# Typical Repair Charges ("Charges" 35098:39328, the intro moved into the hero): 36px between the title and the
   cards, as above the micro price tables. Cards: navy header with the level and its price range (Bold 24/32 white,
   centred as drawn; phones 20/28), Regular 18/28 navy text with Figma's 32px sides (phones 16/24, 20px), three in a
   row from xl, stacked below. The notes follow with the cards' gap. #}
<section class="bg-white" aria-labelledby="charges-title" data-figma="35098:39328">
  <div class="container-page flex flex-col gap-6 py-10 md:gap-9 md:py-[50px]">
    <h2 id="charges-title" class="text-h3 font-medium text-heading md:text-h2 md:font-bold lg:text-h1" data-figma="35098:39329">Typical Repair Charges</h2>
    <div class="flex flex-col gap-4 md:gap-6">
      <ul class="grid gap-4 md:gap-6 xl:grid-cols-3" data-figma="35098:39330">
        {% for lv in cr.levels %}
        <li class="flex min-w-0 flex-col" data-figma="{{ lv.figma }}">
          <h3 class="rounded-t bg-primary-500 px-4 py-3 text-center text-h4 font-bold text-white md:py-4 md:text-h3">{{ lv.name }}: {{ lv.price }}</h3>
          <p class="flex-1 rounded-b border border-t-0 border-outline px-5 py-6 text-base text-primary-500 md:px-8 md:text-lg">{{ lv.text }}</p>
        </li>
        {% endfor %}
      </ul>
      {# Warranty note (35098:39346), the warranty line only as in Figma, as a notice bar so it reads as a condition:
         the outline border with a 4px orange left edge on #f5f8fa, an orange info icon, Medium navy text (Figma's
         orange text is too light on white). Picked from three options on 2026-10-28. #}
      <p class="flex items-center gap-3 rounded border border-l-4 border-outline border-l-accent bg-menu px-4 py-3 text-base font-medium text-heading md:text-lg" data-figma="35098:39346">{% icon "info-square-rounded", "h-6 w-6 text-accent" %}<span>{{ cr.warranty }}</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{ plp_ui.features(cr.seo) }}

{# Disclaimers (35098:39350) as a callout under the features, in the styleguide trust badge's shape (34747:15477:
   52px navy circle with the repair icon, title, text): the brands line as a Bold title, the pricing line and the
   trademark notice under it as fine print. A tinted box with the price tables' outline border, like the other callouts; the text keeps the
   756px reading width. Phones: the circle above the text. #}
<section class="bg-white pb-8 pt-6 md:pb-10" aria-label="Brands we repair" data-figma="35098:39350">
  <div class="container-page">
    <div class="flex flex-col items-start gap-4 rounded border border-outline bg-secondary-100 px-5 py-6 sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:gap-5 md:px-8">
      <span class="flex h-[52px] w-[52px] shrink-0 items-center justify-center rounded-full bg-primary-500 text-white">{% icon "tool", "h-7 w-7" %}</span>
      <div class="flex min-w-0 max-w-[756px] flex-col gap-1">
        <p class="text-base font-bold text-heading md:text-lg">{{ cr.brands }}</p>
        <p class="text-sm text-body">{{ cr.pricingNote }} {{ cr.trademarks }}</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{{ c.faqSection(cr.faq, { section: "35098:39352", list: "35098:39355", card: "34799:68654" }) }}
